Make the ConceptGraphs-Detect imports optional.

Upstream pin: concept-graphs @ 93277a02bd89171f8121e84203121cf7af9ebb5d

ConceptGraphs has two variants (README lines 181-182). The headline one runs SAM in "segment all"
mode and is class-agnostic; ConceptGraphs-Detect adds RAM tagging and GroundingDINO boxes.
generate_gsa_results.py imports both at module scope and constructs GroundingDINO as the first
statement of main(), before it reads --class_set, so the class-agnostic variant cannot run without
building GroundingDINO (a CUDA extension) and installing RAM.

Every Detect-only symbol is confined to branches --class_set none never enters: grounding_dino_model
is used only under detector == "dino", and ram/tag2text only under class_set in (ram, tag2text).
So this changes no line that executes on the path we run.

Without it: the class-agnostic comparison needs the whole Grounded-Segment-Anything stack.
